{
  "title": "Boss: logscan",
  "kind": "boss",
  "summary": "Build a real command-line log scanner: parse, filter by time and level, report with exit codes, and test it with pytest.",
  "minutes": 35,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "The ticket",
      "body": [
        "> **OPS-412** On-call wants one command to answer \"what went wrong in the last two hours?\" across several log files, usable in a terminal and as a CI gate:",
        ">",
        "> `logscan --since 2h --level ERROR app.log worker.log`",
        ">",
        "> Print matching entries oldest first, the count to stderr, and exit `1` when anything matched, `0` when clean, `2` on bad usage or a missing file.",
        "",
        "Every line in these logs looks like `2026-11-26T09:10:00+00:00 ERROR api.db: connection reset`: an ISO 8601 time **with an offset**, a level, a dotted logger name, a colon and the message. You will build it in four parts; each part starts from the previous one."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Part 1: parse a line",
      "prompt": [
        "Write `parse_line(line: str) -> Entry | None` with a frozen dataclass `Entry(ts: datetime, level: str, logger: str, msg: str)`.",
        "",
        "- Use a compiled regex with named groups: `ts`, `level`, `logger` (letters, digits, `_` and dots), then `: ` and the message.",
        "- `level` must be one of `LEVELS = [\"DEBUG\", \"INFO\", \"WARNING\", \"ERROR\", \"CRITICAL\"]`.",
        "- `ts` is parsed with `datetime.fromisoformat` and must be **aware** (have an offset). A naive time, a bad time or a line that does not match gives `None`."
      ],
      "starter": [
        "import re",
        "from dataclasses import dataclass",
        "from datetime import datetime",
        "",
        "LEVELS = [\"DEBUG\", \"INFO\", \"WARNING\", \"ERROR\", \"CRITICAL\"]",
        "",
        "",
        "def parse_line(line: str):",
        "    return None"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "import re",
        "from dataclasses import dataclass",
        "from datetime import datetime",
        "",
        "LEVELS = [\"DEBUG\", \"INFO\", \"WARNING\", \"ERROR\", \"CRITICAL\"]",
        "LINE = re.compile(r\"^(?P<ts>\\S+) (?P<level>[A-Z]+) (?P<logger>[\\w.]+): (?P<msg>.*)$\")",
        "",
        "",
        "@dataclass(frozen=True)",
        "class Entry:",
        "    ts: datetime",
        "    level: str",
        "    logger: str",
        "    msg: str",
        "",
        "",
        "def parse_line(line: str) -> Entry | None:",
        "    m = LINE.match(line.strip())",
        "    if not m or m[\"level\"] not in LEVELS:",
        "        return None",
        "    try:",
        "        ts = datetime.fromisoformat(m[\"ts\"])",
        "    except ValueError:",
        "        return None",
        "    if ts.tzinfo is None:",
        "        return None",
        "    return Entry(ts, m[\"level\"], m[\"logger\"], m[\"msg\"])"
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "from datetime import timezone as _tz, timedelta as _td",
        "_e = parse_line(\"2026-11-26T09:10:00+00:00 ERROR api.db: connection reset: peer closed\")",
        "Dojo.eq(\"fields\", (\"ERROR\", \"api.db\", \"connection reset: peer closed\"), (_e.level, _e.logger, _e.msg) if _e else None)",
        "Dojo.eq(\"an aware time\", datetime(2026, 11, 26, 9, 10, tzinfo=_tz.utc), _e.ts if _e else None)",
        "Dojo.eq(\"an offset is kept\", _td(hours=1), parse_line(\"2026-11-26T10:05:00+01:00 CRITICAL billing: down\").ts.utcoffset())",
        "Dojo.eq(\"a naive time is rejected\", None, parse_line(\"2026-11-26T09:55:00 ERROR api: naive\"))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"an unknown level is rejected\", None, parse_line(\"2026-11-26T09:55:00+00:00 FATAL api: x\"))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"not a log line\", None, parse_line(\"not a log line at all\"))",
        "Dojo.check(\"Entry is frozen\", getattr(Entry, \"__dataclass_params__\").frozen, \"@dataclass(frozen=True)\")"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "`re.compile(r\"^(?P<ts>\\S+) (?P<level>[A-Z]+) (?P<logger>[\\w.]+): (?P<msg>.*)$\")`",
        "`datetime.fromisoformat` raises `ValueError` on garbage; `ts.tzinfo is None` means naive."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Part 2: durations and scanning",
      "prompt": [
        "Keep part 1 and add:",
        "",
        "- `parse_duration(text: str) -> timedelta` for `\"30s\"`, `\"15m\"`, `\"2h\"`, `\"1d\"`; anything else raises `ValueError`.",
        "- `scan(paths: list[Path], since: datetime, level: str) -> list[Entry]`: read each file (UTF-8), keep entries at `level` **or more severe** with `ts >= since`, and return them sorted by time across all files. Comparing aware datetimes with different offsets just works."
      ],
